# Python data models

- Data models are `pydantic.BaseModel` subclasses. Do not use `@dataclass` (or `@dataclasses.dataclass(...)`).
- Do not write classes whose `__init__` only copies its arguments onto `self` (`self.name = name`). Declare the fields on a `BaseModel` instead.

Why: Pydantic gives every model the same validation, serialization and error messages, and removes constructor boilerplate that drifts out of sync with the fields.

## Checks
- enforced-by: prefer-pydantic-over-dataclass
- enforced-by: no-manual-init-boilerplate
